      "writtenOn": "2026-02-10T23:25:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "somewhat optional, depending on whether the suggestion below would make the code easier to work with.\n\nIt seems a bit undesirable to always make two coordinated calls together: first to `consume_next_rows` and then to `get_image_data`.  This requires some extra temporary state (`self.pending_range`) and some `assert`s to enforce.\n\nI assume that you\u0027ve split this into two calls/functions, because FFI is quite limited and doesn\u0027t allow returning more complicated things (e.g. tuples).  Still, I wonder if you could try evaluating if the code could be refactored to just use a single `get_image_data` call that somehow returns both `\u0026[u8]` and `DecodedRowsInfo`.  \"somehow\" can be either:\n\n* Using \"out parameters\" (e.g. `buf: \u0026mut \u0026[u8]`, `rows_info: \u0026mut DecodedRowsInfo`).\n* Or maybe adding `buffer` field to `DecodedRowsInfo` and returning it from `get_image_data`.  This may require making `DecodedRowsInfo\u003c\u0027a\u003e` generic wrt lifetime `\u0027a\u0027, but that seems ok (we already return an `\u0027a`-bound `\u0026[u8]`).\n\nWDYT?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 400,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 400,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "dcd2270d73b02b24de41a66c3a558240ad034e0f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f7dc2a39_04c6f182",
