      "writtenOn": "2026-02-11T09:56:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, in fact I split in two methods exactly because of the limitation I found on FFI not allowing to add byte slices to the returned struct. I have tried both suggested approaches (out Parameter and buffer field in returned struct) and both are feasible, with the only caveat of requiring the method to be marked as unsafe\n\nI think that from API perspected having a single method seems more straight-forward than having to deal with 2 tightly coupled calls. Also, out parameter approach is consistent with next_interlaced_row and read_rwo from rust/png FFI, so I went with that same approach for consistency",
